From 8ec48c81f467e692113ab114e0780fdd84ee2953 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Stammler <seb@oplabs.co>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:13:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: fix three flakes from tests racing each other in one
 process (#181)

* test: write fake commands from a child process, so running one never hits text file busy

Tests that fake `rex`, `herdr`, `hc`, `gh` and `herdr-app` wrote the script with
std::fs::write and then ran it. A fork on another test thread while the file was
open inherited the write handle until that child exec'd, and exec of the script
failed with ETXTBSY in the meantime: rex::agent's tests failed this way about 1 in
80 runs of the module alone. `test_support::write_script` has /bin/sh write the
file, so this process never holds it open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* test(hangup): a finished stdin hangs up even while a forking child holds its writer

The piped-stdin test closed a pipe writer and asserted the reader hung up.
A child that another test is spawning holds a copy of every descriptor
between fork and exec, so the writer could outlive the drop and the pipe
not hang up yet. A socket pair stands in: shutting the writer down hangs
the reader up however many copies stay open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* test(hangup): open the pty controller close-on-exec from the start

pty() opened the controller with openpt and set close-on-exec afterwards.
A child that another test spawned in between (e.g. the delivery test's
`sleep 5 &`) kept the controller past its exec, so the tty did not hang
up within the neighbouring test's 5 s deadline. Opening /dev/ptmx with
O_CLOEXEC closes that window on Linux and macOS alike.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* test(pi): a closed port that no parallel bind(0) can be handed

closed_port() bound port 0 and released it, so a test running alongside could be given the same port and find the "closed" session answering. Port 1 lies below every ephemeral range.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* test: the review crate's and the integration tests' fake commands are written from a child too

The same text file busy race as in the app's unit tests: the review crate's fake gh, and the fake gh, rex, hc and herdr-app of tests/pr_review.rs and tests/rex_hc_review.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* docs(agents): how tests sharing one process stay out of each other's way

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

